 "doc": "DGN-1683 WP1 exhaustive mint verb state table (grill fix 6). The verb emits ONLY these rows; mint_flow.emit() fails closed to BLOCKED for anything else. screen_delivered is true iff note is SCREEN_SENT_END_TURN. agent_utterance: 'none' = say nothing beyond ending the turn; 'N13' = the agent may say the one approved fallback sentence (screen delivery could not be confirmed) and nothing else. State DELIVERY_PENDING, IDLE, BLOCKED and NOT_IMPLEMENTED are emission-only; flow_states are the states persisted in config/mint-flow.json (DELIVERY_PENDING is the emitted view of any flow whose current screen is unconfirmed). agent_utterance 'EXPLAIN' (DGN-1698) = no screen was sent and the owner must not be left in silence: the agent says, in its own words, the emission's explain.why and explain.next (no fixed owner copy). DGN-1702 (dec-182): a make-open starts in WAIT_CONTEXT (nothing sent) and the agent asks, in its own words, what situation the new agent is for; the catalog follows only after the owner's context is recorded. agent_utterance 'consult' (note ASK_OWNER, only on the emission that enters or extends WAIT_CONTEXT; a later status in WAIT_CONTEXT is WAITING_ON_OWNER/'none' because the question is already out) = ask that question (or one follow-up); fact answers_left = owner answers still accepted before the next one closes the consult. The consult close never decides fit by substring: the closing `next` needs --fit <pack_id>|none (BLOCKED/FIT_REQUIRED, nothing written, fact packs = id/name_ko/tagline_ko per eligible pack; an unknown id is INPUT_NOT_ACCEPTED, nothing written); --fit none ends as NO_FIT. 'no_fit' = tell the owner in your own words that no ready agent fits what they described; 'occupied' = tell the owner an agent for this already exists (emission fact occupied.agent), point to it and stop. Each utterance code is a machine-granted permission to speak at that moment; 'none' stays silence. DGN-1702 round 3 (owner rehearsal 2026-09-26): a make-open with request words carries the agent's --fit judged from the request: one pack id -> the catalog goes out at once (WAIT_CHOICE/SCREEN_SENT_END_TURN; needs a confirm --lead; a single-pack card ends with the owner-approved free-text invitation), several ids (comma-joined) -> those candidates, 'consult' -> WAIT_CONTEXT/ASK_OWNER (the ambiguous case only), 'none' -> CANCELLED/NO_FIT; missing -> BLOCKED/FIT_REQUIRED. The lead is judged once when the step is recorded and rendered verbatim in the card's own message. Owner free words at a catalog are a consult answer (the agent re-judges --fit or asks with --more); an expiry/restart button tap is never kept as a consult answer (WAIT_CONTEXT: ASK_OWNER again; WAIT_CHOICE: INPUT_NOT_ACCEPTED). DGN-1844: WAIT_TOKEN -> FAILED_EMPTY is the accepted-token failure before any build starts (the build plan cannot be resolved; reason build_plan_failed): nothing was created, the owner gets the problem screen N11 and a new open starts over.",
